---
title: Proposition 19
---
order: 19
---
short_label: VI.19
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
----
statement: Similar triangles are to one another in the duplicate ratio of the corresponding sides.
----
----
proof:

Let {ABC|ABCt} and {DEF|DEFt} be similar triangles having the angle at {B|angB} equal to the angle at {E|angE}, and such that {AB} is to {BC} as {DE} is to {EF}, so that {BC} corresponds to {EF}. [!just V.Def.11]

I say that  the triangle {ABC|ABCt} has to the triangle {DEF|DEFt} a ratio duplicate of that which {BC} has to {EF}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="330" height="220" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.19 diagram" src="propVI19.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure draws the similar triangles ABC and DEF (random faces)
    // with B, C, E, F on one line, the third proportional BG (G derived,
    // proportion) and the join AG.
